LLD 21's driver snapshots the CPU count before the parallel executor is
created. A growing affinity mask can give that executor more threads than
there are relocation shards, so getThreadIndex() indexes outside relocsVec.
Size the shards from the executor that supplies those indices. Preserve the
single-threaded path, which executes on the main thread without an executor.

LLVM 23 removes implicit thread-index shards altogether in:
https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/905f654bb721f1df119bd2cfaa23736e30838e90
That change depends on the newer RelocScan API and does not apply to LLVM 21.
Remove this patch when the pinned linker includes that upstream change.

--- a/ELF/SyntheticSections.cpp
+++ b/ELF/SyntheticSections.cpp
@@ -4785,1 +4785,3 @@
-  const unsigned threadCount = ctx.arg.threadCount;
+  const unsigned threadCount = parallel::strategy.ThreadsRequested == 1
+                                   ? 1
+                                   : parallel::getThreadCount();
